le-frame live sets; the correction ports the Python fixture's protocol (run to normal completion, collect from the cycle-rooted generator alone); the heap-fixture round dispatched to codex.\norchestrator-logs/1793289946-yang-antlr-call-spec.md:8:Done: Added proposed shared calling convention in section 8.10 and reconciled adjacent references in sections 8.1, 8.5.6 and 8.11. No implementation or separate design document. Existing unrelated orchestrator logs left untouched.\norchestrator-logs/1793203595-jolt-j4d-j5-orchestration.md:131:  duplication — J4d's to reconcile).\norchestrator-logs/1793203595-jolt-j4d-j5-orchestration.md:134:  dao.star. The J3/J4 label drift reconciled.\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_verification.edn:3: :branch \"yang-hardening2\"\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:1:# Session log — yang.clojure track (hardening + adoption of §8.10 common call)\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:5:Prior logs (historical claims, never appended): orchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md,\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:6:orchestrator-logs/1793187400000-glm-yang-clojure-hardening.md, orchestrator-logs/1793188658-yang-clojure-hardening-claude.md\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:13:Done: Re-read docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md (scope of judgment, coordination contract, commit authority, artifact protocol, Workflow 1-11) per the owner's instruction. Re-derived state from the real tree: master stable at 63674368; this track's three branches are pushed and untouched by the repair — yang-common-call@0a15d053 (adoption fix round: codex 1eb14d06 + kimi 0a15d053), yang-hardening2@4c914c05 (hardening-2 arity correction), yang-slice9@7dc18478 (the BLOCKED kernel gate, preserved deliberately).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:24:Done: (1) All three track branches rebased onto the repaired master (ledger conflicts resolved by the union rule both times: 140 and 130 rows, zero markers) and re-verified: adoption 127/1273 + oracle 21/971; hardening-2 suites 122/1338 with its oracle correctly :blocked (20 unexercised arities — the expected state, not a pass). (2) glm confirmation round (session 346a33f5; note its collab/ writes were DENIED so the report lived only in stdout — extracted to findings): ALL SIX original findings CLOSED with its own re-run probes, eligibility follow-up VERIFIED, plus two new P2s: N1 (yang.call/invoke + invoke-with are native-name? operators that bypass the admission witness — a forged assoc map runs; forged scalar/guest-fn entries surface a raw host defect) and N2 (closure manifests missing call.cljc; dao.host.gate-test red on all three lanes). (3) Escalated N1 to the section architect (kimi r5, session_0cbe7179): ruling = witness-gate both operators at the compile branch like yang.call/eligible?; a ledger deviation would contradict r4(a); no shared-runtime change needed; N2 is mechanical. (4) N1/N2 fix round to kimi -> committed 12feb7d1 (gate both operators, refusal/positive/dynamic-eligibility/non-symbol fixtures, three closure manifests regenerated + gate totals updated, dao.host.gate-test adjustments). Verified this seat: 142/1472 across the five suites incl. dao.host.gate-test, oracle 21/971, kondo clean; ran the two N1 fixtures by name (7 and 16 assertions green).\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:760:                 (js/vconj (js/vconj [] (js/callable? foreign))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:762:                 (js/callable? disabled))))]\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:1188:                         (data/callable? (yang.call/entry f))\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:1317:(deftest test-common-call-source-admission\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:2229:(deftest test-hardening-library-admissions\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
