{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/agents/roles/architect.md; sed -n '1930,2140p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; sed -n '1280,1435p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Lead System Architect\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\n\nRead first:\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\n- <target-design-file>\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\n\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\n```\n   #{symbol}}` opts into the argument-vector convention: `:native` names the\n   primitives a bare symbol may call directly (a set, or a map from name to\n   its published profile, whose `:yin.k/arities` give an adapter its admitted\n   counts), `:macros` the expander-side\n   macro names whose calls must stay ordinary applications. The program's\n   own top-level definitions are never native. `:outcomes true` adds the\n   outcome model (see its section); `:adapters` maps a primitive that\n   declares domain failures to the host adapter returning its outcome.\"\n  [forms opts]\n  (if-not opts\n    {}\n    (do (when-not (= :arg-vector (:convention opts))\n          (reject! \"Unknown compile-program convention\" {:opts opts}))\n        (when-let [hit (seq (filter control-heads (:macros opts)))]\n          (reject! \"A :macros entry names a compiler form\" {:macros (vec hit)}))\n        (let [defined (into #{}\n                            (keep (fn [f]\n                                    (when (and (seq? f)\n                                               (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first f))\n                                               (symbol? (second f)))\n                                      (strip-symbol-meta (second f)))))\n                            forms)]\n          ;; the compiler emits bare conj and vec (collection literals, apply),\n          ;; so a program definition of either would capture them\n          (when-let [hit (first (filter #{'conj 'vec} defined))]\n            (reject! (str \"Defining \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n                     {:name hit}))\n          (cond-> {::convention {:native (set (if (map? (:native opts))\n                                                (keys (:native opts))\n                                                (:native opts)))\n                                 :arities (into {}\n                                                (keep (fn [[sym profile]]\n                                                        (when-let [a (if (map? profile)\n                                                                       (:yin.k/arities profile)\n                                                                       profile)]\n                                                          [sym a])))\n                                                (when (map? (:native opts)) (:native opts)))\n                                 :macros (set (:macros opts))}\n                   ::defined defined\n                   ::invoker (boolean (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defn (first %))\n                                                  (= 'invoke-value (second %))\n                                                  (:yin.k/invoker (meta (second %)))) forms))}\n            (:outcomes opts) (assoc ::outcomes {:adapters (or (:adapters opts) {})}))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-program-symbols!\n  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form)\n    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when (and (nil? (namespace form)) (contains? #{'loop 'recur} form))\n          (reject! (str form \" is only legal in operator position\") {:symbol form})))\n    (seq? form)\n    (when-not (= 'quote (first form))\n      (let [head (first form)]\n        (when (and (symbol? head) (reserved-name? head))\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol head, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when-not (symbol? head)\n          (check-program-symbols! head))\n        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\n    (map? form) (run! check-program-symbols! (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n    (coll? form) (run! check-program-symbols! form)))\n\n\n(defn- check-top-level-discard!\n  \"Only the last top-level form's outcome reaches the harness, so a non-final,\n   non-definition form that may fail would have its error silently discarded:\n   refuse it, as a def value that calls guest functions is refused. Returns\n   `form`.\"\n  [env macro-env forms form]\n  (when (and (next forms)\n             (not (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form))))\n             (failing? (assoc env ::macro-env macro-env) (rewrite-ex-info form)))\n    (reject! \"A non-final top-level form that may fail would discard its error outcome\"\n             {:form form}))\n  form)\n\n\n(defn- lower-top-form\n  \"Under the outcome model a top-level expression returns an outcome like a\n   function body; definitions keep their own lowering.\"\n  [env macro-env form]\n  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n    form\n    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n\n\n(defn compile-program\n  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n  ([forms tail? opts]\n   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles its\n     ;; paths at each definition during machine-data validation and UCF lift.\n     (letfn [(discard-result\n               [ast]\n               (if (outcomes? env) (u/then ast (u/lit nil)) ast))\n             (go\n               [forms macro-env]\n               (if (empty? forms)\n                 (compile-literal nil tail?)\n                 (let [head       (cond->> (first forms)\n                                    (outcomes? env) (check-top-level-discard! env macro-env forms)\n                                    (outcomes? env) (lower-top-form env macro-env))\n                       rest-forms (rest forms)]\n                   (cond\n                     ;; defmacro: ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax whose\n                     ;; lambda the encoder declares; later forms see the name\n                     ;; only so the native defn lowering can yield to it.\n                     (and (seq? head) (= 'defmacro (first head)))\n                     (let [defined (compile-defmacro (rest head) env false macro-env)]\n                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                           :body (go rest-forms\n                                                     (assoc macro-env\n                                                            (strip-symbol-meta (second head))\n                                                            {:type :user}))}\n                                :operands [(discard-result defined)]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; def: sequence with current macro-env\n                     (and (seq? head) (= 'def (first head)))\n                     (let [[_ name value] head\n                           value (cond-> value (outcomes? env) rewrite-ex-info)]\n                       (when (and (outcomes? env)\n                                  (failing? (assoc env ::macro-env macro-env) value))\n                         (reject! \"A def value cannot call guest functions under the outcome model\"\n                                  {:name name}))\n                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                           :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                                :operands [(discard-result (compile-def name value env false macro-env))]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; single form\n                     (= 1 (count forms))\n                     (compile-form head tail? (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env)\n                     ;; sequence\n                     :else\n                     (cond-> {:type     :application\n                              :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                         :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                              :operands [(discard-result\n                                           (compile-form head false\n                                                         (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n       (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                           'dsg__admitted?\n                           (u/sexp->uast\n                             '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n                                  (let [dsg__entry (dsg__get dsg__candidate :yang.call/entry)\n                                        dsg__witness (dsg__get dsg__candidate :clj/admission)]\n                                    (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n                                      (dsg__equal\n                                        dsg__witness\n                                        (dsg__make_admission\n                                          (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate :clj/admission nil)))\n                                      false))\n                                  false))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                           'dsg__make_admission\n                           (u/sexp->uast\n                             '(fn [dsg__descriptor]\n                                (fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                  (if (data/callable? dsg__call_token)\n                                    (dsg__get dsg__descriptor :yang.call/entry)\n                                    nil)))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/then\n                           (discard-result\n                             (u/app (u/lam '[get = assoc empty?] call/uast)\n                                    (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                    (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v 'dsg__empty))))\n         (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__call_token (u/lam [] (u/lit nil)))\n         ;; Guest closures keep captured environments portable: binding host\n         ;; primitive values here would make UCF machine-data validation fail.\n         ;; These helpers cover generated map lookups/writes and comparisons;\n         ;; conj/vec are already protected by the convention's binder checks.\n         ;; Evaluate siblings outside each other's bindings to avoid retaining\n         ;; a chain of redundant helper environments.\n         (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                             (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n                             (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 '(fn [m k]\n                                    (if (data/map? m)\n                                      (let [find (fn [self entries]\n                                                   (if (data/content= 0 (data/count entries))\n                                                     nil\n                                                     (let [pair (data/nth entries 0)]\n                                                       (if (data/content= k (data/nth pair 0))\n                                                         (data/nth pair 1)\n                                                         (self self (data/subvec entries 1))))))]\n                                        (find find (vec m)))\n                    (fn [node]\n                      (if (= node (u/v 'profile-raise))\n                        (u/lam ['condition] (u/lit :refused))\n                        node))\n                    (outcome-ast (if admitted?\n                                   ['(defn f [x] (+ x 21)) invoke]\n                                   [invoke])))\n              _ (reset! effect-log [])\n              [result] (run ast)]\n          (is (= expected @effect-log) (str operator \" admitted=\" admitted?))\n          (when admitted?\n            (is (= [:yin.k/ok 42] result) (str operator))))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-shadowed-helpers\n  (doseq [binding '[get = assoc empty?]]\n    (testing (str \"construction and invocation with a local \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 21]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'let [binding 5]\n                                 '(let [f (fn [x] x)] (f 21)))]))))\n    (testing (str \"a later source definition of \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 21]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'def binding 5) '(defn f\n                                                    [x]\n                                                    x) '(f 21)]))))\n    (testing (str \"raise through a parameter named \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"boom\", :yin.k/data {:x 21}}]\n             (run-outcome\n               ['(defn g\n                   []\n                   (throw (ex-info \"boom\" {:x 21})))\n                (list 'defn 'f [binding] '(g))\n                '(+ 1 (f 5))])))))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok 1]\n         (run-outcome '[(def f (let [get 5] (fn [x] x))) (f 1)]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-source-admission\n  (doseq [form '[(let [x 5] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:ordinary :map}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry 5}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:py/type :function :code :legacy}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry 5}] ((if true x x) 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc {} :yang.call/entry (get f :yang.call/entry))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc f :extra :forged)] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc f :yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry g))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc {} :yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)\n                                :clj/admission (get f :clj/admission))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)\n                          :clj/admission (fn [x] true)}] (x 1))]]\n    (doseq [wrap [identity #(list '+ 1 %)]]\n      (let [result (run-outcome ['(defn f\n                                    [x]\n                                    x)\n                                 '(defn g\n                                    [x]\n                                    (+ x 1)) (wrap form)])]\n        (is (= :yin.k/error (first result)) (pr-str form))\n        (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason (second result)))\n            (pr-str form)))))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok [false false true 21]]\n         (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                          [x]\n                          x)\n                        [(yang.call/eligible? {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)})\n                         (yang.call/eligible? (assoc f :extra :forged))\n                         (yang.call/eligible? f)\n                         (f 21)]]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-invalid-continuation-refuses\n  (let [ast (walk/postwalk\n              (fn [node]\n                (if (= node u/capture) (u/lit :invalid-continuation) node))\n              (outcome-ast '[(defn f\n                               []\n                               1) (+ 1 (f))]))]\n    (doseq [run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n      (let [result (first (run ast))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/error (first result)))\n        (is (= {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                :yang.call/data {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}}\n               (second result)))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-rejects-named-arguments\n  (let [forms '[(defn f\n                  [x]\n                  x)\n                (let [condition (yang.call/invoke f [] [[\"x\" 1]] profile-raise)\n                      value (get condition :yang.call/value)]\n                  [(get condition :yang.call/reason)\n                   (get value :yin.k/message)\n                   (get (get value :yin.k/data) :yang.call/named)])]\n        raw-raise (fn [node]\n                    (if (= node (u/v 'profile-raise)) (u/v 'probe/note) node))\n        ast (walk/postwalk raw-raise (outcome-ast forms))\n        result (-> (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules outcome-modules}))\n                   (tu/queue-ast! ast)\n                   tu/run-session\n                   :consumer\n                   vm/value)]\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok\n            [:yang.call/thrown\n             \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\"\n             [[\"x\" 1]]]]\n           result))))\n\n\n(deftest test-outcome-safe-get\n  (let [forms '[(defn safe-get\n                  [coll key]\n                  (let [val (get coll key)]\n                    (if val val (throw (ex-info \"No such value in collection\" {:coll coll, :key key})))))]]\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok 1] (run-outcome (conj forms '(safe-get {:a 1} :a)))))\n    (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"No such value in collection\"\n                          :yin.k/data {:coll {:a 1}, :key :b}}]\n           (run-outcome (conj forms '(safe-get {:a 1} :b)))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-outcome-nested-call-operand\n  (let [defs '[(defn g\n                 [x]\n                 (if x x (throw (ex-info \"g failed\" {:x x}))))\n               (defn h\n                 [x]\n                 x)]\n        failed [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"g failed\", :yin.k/data {:x nil}}]]\n    (testing \"an error in an operand of a nested call ends the caller\"\n      (is (= failed (run-outcome (into defs '[(defn f\n                                                [x]\n                                                (+ 1 (g x))) (f nil)]))))\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 6] (run-outcome (into defs '[(defn f\n                                                       [x]\n                                                       (+ 1 (g x))) (f 5)]))))\n      (is (= failed (run-outcome (into defs '[(defn f\n                                                [x]\n                                                (h (h (g x)))) (f nil)])))\n          \"through two enclosing calls\"))\n    (testing \"operands evaluate left to right and stop at the first failure\"\n      (is (= [failed [:a]]\n             [(run-outcome (into defs '[(defn f\n                                          [x]\n                                          [(probe/note :a) (g x) (probe/note :b)])\n                                        (f nil)]))\n              @effect-log])))))\n\n\n(deftest test-outcome-mid-do-stops-later-effects\n  (let [forms '[(defn boom\n                  []\n                  (throw (ex-info \"stop\" {})))\n                (defn run\n                  []\n                  (do (probe/note :before) (boom) (probe/note :after) :done))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
